id: pm-vcs-wm40
title: "Phase 3: distribution over a real transport"
description: "Bundles let two repositories exchange history offline, which is enough to prove the object model but is not distribution. This phase adds named remotes, remote-tracking refs, and clone, fetch and push over a transport, with object negotiation computed from reachability rather than sending the whole store, and non-fast-forward pushes refused by default."
type: Epic
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:28:24.061Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-02T21:36:35.505Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-02T21:36:35.486Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-02T21:36:35.486Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: pm vcs clone produces a repository whose object closure and refs are identical to the source; fetch transfers only objects the receiver lacks; push refuses a non-fast-forward without an explicit override and never leaves a ref pointing at an object that was not transferred; remote-tracking refs live under refs/remotes and are never confused with local branches; Repository and branch identities remain stable across rename archive and restore operations; An interrupted missing-object upload resumes by transferring only absent verified objects; The receiver rejects publication until the uploaded object closure is complete and hash-valid; Peers negotiate supported capabilities and repository format versions before transferring data and reject incompatible peers without changing refs; Bundles and fully local repositories remain usable without a configured or reachable remote; The remote ref advances only through one final compare-and-swap and a lost race leaves both local history and the winner remote tip intact while reporting retryable publication failure
